# Development tooling

Use the supported Node 24.16.0 / Yarn 4.17.0 baseline and `package.json` scripts.
`yarn dev` is Astro on 3000; `yarn preview` exposes only the validated `dist/public`
artifact on 4173. Stop a manual preview before `yarn test:e2e`.

`yarn build` explicitly chains verification, static generation into `dist/site-build`
and public preparation. Preparation also synchronizes local `firebase.json` CSP
hashes; it does not contact the provider. `yarn verify` runs Astro/TypeScript,
contrast/gamut and focused unit/fixture tests. Required stages stay explicit because
Yarn 4 does not auto-run custom pre/post hooks.

The two narrowly scoped `.yarnrc.yml` checker-manifest repairs have actual import
and peer evidence. Follow the toolchain notes in `docs/operations/publication.md`
before changing them. Unused Firebase compatibility-package peer warnings are
qualified in `src/lib/firebase/README.md`.

Normal builds never write root output. Retained Vite `legacy:build`, `prerender`,
`clean` and `sync:static` do; preserve `emptyOutDir: false` and use them only in a
reviewed recovery. Publication and rollback default to preview, verify exact
ownership and preserve unrelated files. Follow the publication runbook for any apply.
